Action Order
The full order of actions and events throughout a night.
<BOLD>Night 1 only :</BOLD>
• <TOWN>Bakers</TOWN>, <TOWN>Butchers</TOWN> wake
• <TOWN>Fletcher</TOWN> selects <EXTRA>Fletcher's Customer</EXTRA>
• <UA>Cupid</UA> selects <EXTRA>Cupid's Lover</EXTRA>
• <UA>Thief</UA> switches role
• <UA>Chef</UA> sees waiters
<BOLD>Night 2 only :</BOLD>
• <TOWN>Amnesiac</TOWN> changes role
• <WOLF>Infecting Werewolf</WOLF> selects target (consider <TOWN>Devout   Villager</TOWN>)
<BOLD>Each night:</BOLD>
• <ELECTED>Reporter</ELECTED> wakes and see the cards of the newly dead
• For advanced players, town sided groups wake in the following order: <TOWN>Bakers</TOWN>, <TOWN>Butchers</TOWN>
• <TOWN>Stalker</TOWN> wakes and chooses a target
• <TOWN>Fletcher</TOWN> wakes and may revoke the customer's power
• <WOLF>Alpha Werewolf</WOLF> wakes and may use a howl
• <UW>Vampire</UW> wakes and chooses a player to demonize, the <UW>Undead</UW> wake with the vampire
• <FLUTE>Flute Player</FLUTE> wakes and enchants, afterward all <EXTRA>Enchanted</EXTRA> players wake
• <HELL>Devil</HELL> wakes and chooses a player, afterward the <EXTRA>Deal Recipient</EXTRA> wakes
• Investigative roles wake in the following order: <TOWN>Oracle</TOWN>, <TOWN>Aura Teller</TOWN>, <TOWN>Huntsman</TOWN>, <TOWN>Seer</TOWN>, <TOWN>Apprentice</TOWN>, <TOWN>Town Crier</TOWN>, <WOLF>Warlock</WOLF>, <WOLF>Mystic Fox</WOLF>
• Protective roles wake in the following order: <TOWN>Cleric</TOWN>, <TOWN>Hooker</TOWN>, <WOLF>Gallant Fox</WOLF>, <UA>Chef</UA>, <ELECTED>Guardian</ELECTED>
• Killing roles wake in the following order: <TOWN>Assassin</TOWN> (Night 2 onwards), <TOWN>Priest</TOWN>, <PYRO>Pyromancer</PYRO>
• The <WOLF>Werewolves</WOLF> wake together (and receive fox info if applicable). They choose somebody to attack. If a <WOLF>Wolf Cub</WOLF> has died or if a striking howl has been used they choose a second time.
• <TOWN>Witch</TOWN> wakes and chooses whether to protect/kill.
• On even nights the <WWW>White Werewolf</WWW> also wakes
• <WOLF>Psychic Werewolf</WOLF> wakes and checks a player's role